UND_SERVICE"}, {"name": "android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MICROPHONE"}, {"name": "android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC"}, {"name": "android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS"}, {"name": "android.permission.WAKE_LOCK"}, {"name": "com.freedomfighter.readersnotes.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION"}]}}}}, "com.freedomfighter.readersphone": {"metadata": {"lastUpdated": 1793024891000, "description": {"en-US": "A call rings on the whole screen with the person's photo and name and two big buttons;\nmissed calls stay at the top until answered with \"call back\" or \"OK\". Contacts read\nfavourites, then the people called lately, then everyone; a keypad with large keys; the\nlist of calls. Leave the call for another app and it stays in view: Android's own call\nnotification with one big \"hang up\", and a wide green band that brings the call back.\n\nRecording (off by default): a call is recorded and written out on the phone by\nwhisper.cpp, the model fetched once and shared with the other Reader's apps. Android only\ngives the sound of a call to an accessibility service, so one has to be switched on; the\nsettings say so. Tell the other person — in many countries the law requires it.\n\nUnknown callers (off by default): a number nobody in the contacts has is looked up in\nthe Swiss directory of search.ch, with your own free key for private use pasted in the\nsettings; only that number leaves the phone. Data: Swisscom Directories AG.\n\nSix languages. No account; the network is used only to fetch the model and, when you ask\nfor it, the directory.\n"}}, "versions": {"b8760515733d53927da7c61f881b865ffd39911ec7bb95822b73aff5577dca4e": null, "d068f8585417b94923a0c3dcfc3343afcd031caa6a8620eedb9c5aa7efe00622": {"added": 1793024891000, "file": {"name": "/ReadersPhone-v1.6.0.apk", "sha256": "d068f8585417b94923a0c3dcfc3343afcd031caa6a8620eedb9c5aa7efe00622", "size": 36230845}, "manifest": {"nativecode": ["arm64-v8a", "x86_64"], "versionName": "1.6.0", "versionCode"